        mlt:citation "Thompson, D.W. (1917) On Growth and Form. Cambridge University Press. Ch. IV, pp. 156-200, Figs. 58-59." ;
        mlt:claim "Early cleavage/segmentation patterns of eggs conform to the same bipolar (two-like-pole) field configuration." ;
        mlt:claimId "T1917-012" ;
        mlt:counterclaim "No direct literature test of Thompson's two-like-pole field reading of cleavage patterns. The modern mechanism (spindle position -> cleavage furrow) makes the field picture unnecessary, which is a supersession by neglect, not a refutation." ;
        mlt:dataKindNeeded "embryo cleavage imaging" ;
